keeping button mounted is necessary. But perhaps the showClear state should remain true until blur? The diff leaves it forever, so button always visible after first input. Is that intended? It says non-empty query shows button; doesn't explicitly say empty query hides button. But \"clearing ... leaves focus on that button\" means it remains. It may be acceptable to keep it mounted while focused; but after user tabs away, it should probably disappear. Not in criteria. Could mention not fail? We need choose FAIL only concrete. The empty task list is stronger.\n\nAnother bug: query trim. If user enters spaces only, normalizedQuery empty, visible all tasks, but showClear true (because value !== ''). So non-empty query (spaces) shows Clear search button, but filtering not applied because trim empty. Is that okay? \"Filtering immediate and case-insensitive against task titles.\" A query of spaces arguably normalizes to empty. But \"non-empty query shows Clear search\"; space is non-empty. Clear visible yes. Fine.\n\n`showClear` initialized false. If user types whitespace, showClear true, query whitespace, filter all. Clear button. Fine.\n\nFocus: clearSearch just setQuery(''); button remains because showClear unchanged. React keeps same element (conditional true) no remount, focus stays. Good.\n\nSelection: filtering hides selected row; selectedId remains in App. Detail card derives full tasks? We don't see App but diff only TaskList, doesn't call onSelect. Good.\n\nPotential bug: `showClear` redundant and not derived. After clear, button remains visible. If user clicks elsewhere, still visible with empty query. The requirement only says non-empty shows; doesn't require hide when empty; but UI convention maybe clear button should disappear. But explicit focus on button after clearing forces it to remain at least at that moment. Could be hidden after blur maybe not specified. Not a fail.\n\nAnother issue: \"If no task matches, show exactly `No tasks match your search.`.\" Current code shows empty paragraph when visibleTasks.length === 0. But it removes the `<ul class=\"task-list\">` entirely. Existing behavior? If no tasks visible, list absent. It might be okay. But if query empty and tasks length 0, message wrong. I'd fail on that.\n\nNeed ensure \"Do not modify or delete existing public tests.\" no tests diff. Fine.\n\nNeed provide first line exactly VERDICT: FAIL. Then findings. Need name severity, affected behavior, exact diff evidence, reproduction, bounded fix. We should be concise but satisfy.\n\nWe can mention one finding. Is it concrete and repairable. Yes.\n\nLet's craft: FAIL — empty task list with no active query. Severity medium maybe? It's a regression in empty state messaging. Evidence: `const normalizedQuery = query.trim().toLowerCase();` and `{visibleTasks.length === 0 ? (<p ...>No tasks match your search.</p>) : (...)}`. When tasks=[] and query='', normalizedQuery empty, visibleTasks=tasks=[], so condition true, message shown even with no search. Reproduction: render TaskList with tasks=[] selectedId null onSelect/onEdit no-op; before diff renders empty ul, now \"No tasks match your search.\" This violates preserve existing behavior and misattributes no data to search. Bounded fix: gate search-empty on normalizedQuery and visibleTasks.length === 0; for no tasks and no query render existing empty `<ul className=\"task-list\" />` (or prior empty state) so no search message. Example `const hasNoMatches = normalizedQuery !== '' && visibleTasks.length === 0;` and render empty message only when hasNoMatches, else list. Ensure when query nonempty and tasks empty, message shows exactly. That is bounded.\n\nShould we include showClear remaining visible? Maybe as a secondary PASS comment? Since FAIL, can note no issue? Maybe avoid extra. But the role asks focus. Could mention \"Focus/cancellation/selection appear okay...\" But not necessary. Desired oververbosity 5. Ensure no invented. We can add \"No other blocking issues found in supplied diff.\" But final should be first line exact.\n\nNeed verify if there's any other more concrete bug: When clearing, `showClear` remains true; the button stays. Acceptance: \"A non-empty query shows a Clear search button; clearing restores every task and leaves focus on that button.\" Actually this requires button after clearing, so okay.\n\nBut wait: Focus on button: The clear button uses `className=\"icon-button\"` and text \"Clear search\", no aria-label needed. On clearSearch, setQuery('') triggers re-render; conditional remains true because showClear true, so same button stays mounted. good.\n\nCould there be a bug with `setShowClear(value !== '')` if value spaces: showClear true, but normalized empty; clear visible. Fine.\n\nPotential case-insensitive includes but uses lowercased title; what if title has Turkish? Not relevant.\n\nSelection: if selected task hidden and then query changes such that selected row visible, class selected. Good. Detail card stable because App untouched. Good.\n\nPotential stale selection if tasks change? No.\n\nShould we fail because `showClear` state doesn't reset when query is cleared via input native search clear (the x in type=search)? Input type=search can be cleared by UA? The onChange would set value '', handleQueryChange sets showClear false. Then clear button disappears, but focus? Native x. Acceptance specifically clear button. Not issue.\n\nWhat about pressing Escape in search input? type=search may clear on Escape. Then showClear false. Fine.\n\nThe empty list bug is maybe not a \"critical\" acceptance? \"Preserve all existing behavior\" is acceptance. Existing behavior when tasks empty likely no message. But is that testable? The diff changes existing rendering. It is concrete. Use severity medium.\n\nNeed maybe mention exact line: `const visibleTasks = normalizedQuery ? ... : tasks;` and `visibleTasks.length === 0`. Good.\n\nCould there be a more severe bug: When there are no tasks due to initial load and query is empty, the \"No tasks match your search.\" is wrong and confusing. Yes.\n\nLet's final.","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":"7561dad4-550f-4774-a550-39200c4cf0b5-0","status":"completed"},{"id":"51ca2e0b-004c-49c8-8133-ed719975b70a","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"VERDICT: FAIL\n\n**Finding — Medium: empty task list now shows a search-specific message with no active search**\n\n- Affected behavior: existing empty-list state and acceptance criterion “Preserve all existing behavior.”\n- Diff evidence:\n  - `const normalizedQuery = query.trim().toLowerCase();`\n  - `const visibleTasks = normalizedQuery ? tasks.filter(...) : tasks;`\n  - `{visibleTasks.length === 0 ? (<p className=\"task-search-empty\">No tasks match your search.</p>) : (...) }`\n- Why it fails: when `tasks` is empty and `query` is empty, `normalizedQuery` is empty, `visibleTasks` is empty, so the new empty-search message renders even though the user has not searched. Previously the component rendered the existing task-list structure without a search-specific message. This misreports an empty data state as a search mismatch and changes pre-existing behavior.\n- Reproduction: render `<TaskList tasks={[]} selectedId={null} onSelect={() => {}} onEdit={() => {}} />`. The output now contains exactly `No tasks match your search.` with no query entered.\n- Bounded fix: only show the search-empty message when there is an active normalized query:\n  - `const hasSearch = normalizedQuery !== '';`\n  - show `No tasks match your search.` only when `hasSearch && visibleTasks.length === 0`;\n  - otherwise render the existing list/empty-list behavior, preserving the no-query empty state.\n\nNo other blocking regression is supported by the supplied diff: selection state is not mutated by filtering, and keeping the clear button mounted preserves focus after clearing.","type":"output_text","logprobs":[]}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":"final_answer"}],"timestamp":"2026-11-22T16:07:59.112110+00:00"}],"meta":{"snapshot_version":1,"aid":1,"role":"workflow_agent","model":"deepseek-flash","session_state":{"used_tokens":3830,"context_tokens":1354,"step_count":1,"markup_recovered":0,"recent_call_hashes":[],"reads_since_last_edit":0,"has_landed_write":false,"low_yield_since_progress":0,"distinct_evidence_count":0,"scout_ledger":[],"steps_since_progress":0,"wind_down_done":false,"wind_down_attempts":0,"wind_down_token_mark":0,"budget_reserve_consumed":false,"loop_blocked_since_progress":0,"loop_state":{"version":1,"edit_seq":0,"blocked_rounds":0,"last_counted_step":-1,"operations":{}},"write_effect_unknown":false,"last_progress_unknown":false,"phase":"done","terminal_reason":"completed","pending_events":[],"pending_external_user_turn":null,"active_turn_start_message_index":null,"completed_turn_start_message_index":2,"pending_step_latency":null,"submitted_summary":null,"anthropic_history":null},"run_id":"workflow-6c35c1bb5741498ab91281177852c709"},"seen_result_hashes_reset":false,"seen_result_hashes_added":[]}
